id: pm-github-closeout-attribution
title: Hold ambiguous merged-PR delivery until attribution is verified
description: "Follow up the completed declaration matcher with explicit item delivery links, acceptance-criteria chronology and needs_review candidates; pm-ado issue 33 and PR 32 expose incorrect durable delivery provenance."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: changelog-unreleased,closeout,"gh:unbraind/pm-ado#33"
created_at: "2026-10-24T06:16:55.856Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T15:42:25.657Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Explicit delivery link wins; otherwise exactly one claimed merged PR after the latest criteria change may close; ambiguous items remain open with all candidates reported; completion uses the chosen merge timestamp.
comments[40]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T06:16:59.176Z",codex-agent,"Read pm-ado issue 33 and dirty PR 32. Existing pm-github-uqjf is closed and covers declarations; this follow-up replaces its latest-merge tie-break with explicit delivery attribution and acceptance-history checks. Plan: real non-git tracker regressions, function-only revert proof, focused local gates and npm/Bun CI release gates. PR 32 will be closed with cross-links after the fix PR exists; issue 33 stays open."
  "2026-10-24T06:21:01.545Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit delivery-pr URL tags, immutable SDK acceptance-history cutoff, unique body/commit claims and needs_review rows retaining all candidates. Check success no longer breaks ties or falls back to old delivery. Review-only workflow runs persist a privacy-gated closeout-review.json report and open a PR without closing any item. Initial non-git selection suite passes 13/13; existing chronological tie-break assertions updated to require review. Dependency pins and gate thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T06:24:07.508Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test run passed selection 13/13 with no failures or skips; test-result storage is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment retains the receipt. Independently inspected pm-ado PRs 16 and 19: 16 explicitly leaves statement enforcement open; 19 declares the item and merged at 2026-10-08T01:19:51Z. Added a review-only workflow report; held attribution also disables automatic landing after dispatching caller checks."
  "2026-10-24T06:25:34.878Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only runCloseout with its f4c29e8 origin/main implementation, preserving current helpers and tests. Ran node --test --test-name-pattern='ambiguous linked merged PRs|explicit delivery link selects|a claim before or equal' test/closeout-selection.test.ts. Reverted function: exit 1, 0/3 pass and 3 ERR_ASSERTION failures (ambiguous delivery closed, explicit override ignored, pre-criteria claim closed). Restored function: exit 0, 3/3 pass, no skips. Tests import TypeScript source directly; no dist rebuild is needed. Focused c8 reports closeout.ts at exact 100/100/100/100; one pre-update array-order assertion was corrected and its full attribution/selection suites now pass 25/25."
  "2026-10-24T06:29:51.379Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/174 is ready for review. Closed DIRTY pm-ado PR 32 with links to this fix and pm-ado issue 33; verified state CLOSED with mergedAt null and issue 33 still OPEN. No pm-ado branch or tracker edits. Added a completeness guard: unreadable commit messages on a qualifying linked mention may hide a competing claim, so they hold automatic selection. Narrow guard-only revert made the new regression fail ERR_ASSERTION (closed 1 instead of 0, exit 1); restored guard and pre-criteria negative control pass 2/2."
  "2026-10-24T06:30:38.823Z",codex-agent,"Final focused command node --test test/closeout.test.ts test/closeout-attribution.test.ts test/closeout-selection.test.ts passes 117/117, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Focused c8 measures exact 100/100/100/100 for closeout.ts at the completed implementation. Full workflow suite passes 34/34, plus the updated automatic-landing hold regression passes 1/1. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (201 declarations), zero source duplication, changelog checks and clean-environment strict tracker health pass. Initial CI is running on the earlier source commit; final npm/Bun release-gate evidence will be reported in PR 174 checks and body after this last implementation update. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-24T06:42:48.829Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40070500891 exposed three cross-suite fixture/contract failures: Node 26 release gate ran 1121 tests, 1118 passed and 3 failed; all authored sources still measured exact 100/100/100/100. Two changelog-placement fixtures create the item after the synthetic delivery date; the maintenance equality assertion does not account for the new closeout-only attribution hold. Correcting fixture chronology with the deterministic SDK clock and preserving exact parity for the remaining maintenance shell. This failed run is not full-gate approval."
  "2026-10-24T06:43:28.268Z",codex-agent,"Cross-suite corrections pass: node --test test/bot-pr-workflow.test.ts test/changelog-placement.test.ts = 59/59, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Changelog fixtures now create items with a deterministic September SDK clock before October delivery; commit evidence correctly returns an empty list. The parity assertion requires exactly one closeout attribution-hold block and exact equality for all remaining maintenance code. Existing end-to-end review-only acceptance proves this hold dispatches checks without enabling automatic landing. Test typecheck and lint pass. Runtime source remains identical to 8b0dc30; full CI will rerun on the corrected test head."
  "2026-10-24T07:46:02.118Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 174: retain every plausible linked merged candidate independently of evidence quality, report evidence gaps and hold ambiguity before mutation; disarm reused workflow PRs before updates and on all exit paths. Add table-driven real-tracker and stateful workflow regressions, record fix-only revert proofs, then run targeted checks and unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Remote branch is current and contains origin/main."
  "2026-10-24T07:53:26.797Z",codex-agent,"Class 1 revert proof: replaced only runCloseout with the pre-round implementation, retained current helpers and regression table, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"incomplete candidate holds attribution\" test/closeout-selection.test.ts. Exit 1 with assertion failures, including 1 closure instead of 0 for missing merge SHA plus another valid claim; fetch-error cases also exposed the prior abort instead of a listed hold. Restored runCloseout. The full restored selection suite passed 35/35, zero failures, cancellations or skips. Class 2 revert proof: replaced only both explicit --disable-auto operations with no-ops, retained the workflow and stateful harness, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"earlier armed auto-merge is disabled\" test/closeout-workflow.test.ts. Exit 1 with ERR_ASSERTION true !== false: the earlier request remained armed after the later hold. Restored both disable operations. Further restored-suite validation is in progress."
  "2026-10-24T08:00:32.158Z",codex-agent,"Evidence-gap rows now preserve all candidate numbers and list missing fields/codes in compact output and the privacy-gated workflow artifact. Unknown merged status/time is not a chronology exclusion; a failed PR read conservatively holds eligible active items because linkage cannot be disproved. The workflow revokes before any guard or update and always cleans up after hold, no publication, disabled CI, failure or cancellation; initial revocation denial blocks publication. Reviewed all exit classes and documented the audit. Maintenance/changelog contracts passed 59/59; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication passed. Focused coverage measured 100/100/100/100 before the final merge-field reporting helper; full gates will certify the final source. A new parent-scope control correctly held the eligible child as well, so its assertion now checks that the parent is absent from review rows."
  "2026-10-24T08:08:32.103Z",codex-agent,"Additional class 1 pagination proof: PR commit totals now certify the complete commit-page set. Missing, invalid or mismatched counts hold candidates, including a body mention whose omitted commit could claim delivery. Removed only the commit-count completeness guard and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"incomplete candidate holds attribution: .*commits-count\" test/closeout-selection.test.ts: 4/4 failed, exit 1, including 1 closure instead of 0 with another valid claim. Restored the guard. The stateful hold regression and unarmed-PR control pass 2/2 after filtering actual autoMergeRequest state; the corrected fresh-job no-op control passes 1/1. The harness keeps remote PR state across runs and resets only job environment state, matching Actions semantics. Final npm gate is being restarted for this complete pagination fix; prior interrupted gates are not counted as evidence."
  "2026-10-24T08:10:08.391Z",codex-agent,"Final candidate table contains 20 disqualifying evidence conditions crossed with another valid claim or none (40 cases). The pinned pm linked selection run passed 59/59 before the two negative-count controls were added; those additional controls passed 2/2 separately. Final compiled workflow hold/unarmed/no-op acceptance passed 3/3. The 59-test maintenance/changelog contract suite passed; final typecheck, test typecheck and lint passed. Full npm release-check is running on the complete source and test set, with unchanged thresholds, pins and coverage inventory. Origin main has not advanced. No PM CLI/SDK defect was found; linked test storage remains disabled by existing project policy, so comments retain the receipts."
  "2026-10-24T08:28:53.542Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40076990035 at e795426: both bun run release:check jobs (Node 22 and 26) completed successfully, each 1177/1177 tests, zero failures and exact 100/100/100/100 across 19 authored modules. Both Complete npm release gate steps also succeeded; their jobs are now running additional native Bun acceptance, so overall CI is not yet approval. The independent local npm gate has completed 1177/1177 tests with zero failures and is finishing coverage/release processing. The final small source change makes the new commit-count property optional for callers of checkCloseoutHead, preserving the head-check API; decoded closeout PRs still require verified totals. Typecheck and test typecheck passed with this compatibility adjustment. Implementation is complete; remaining work is read-only final CI verification. Final receipts will be retained in PR 174 body and the handoff summary. The tracker item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-24T09:04:43.750Z",codex-agent,"Final consistency review found a report-state defect in the new unreadable-PR path: an explicit valid delivery tag can resolve attribution and close its item, while the non-selected unreadable PR retains an initial needs_review action without candidate details. Initialize that row as a refusal until attribution is resolved, as for all other candidate rows; unresolved groups still promote every row to needs_review. Add a real-tracker regression that a resolved explicit link cannot leave a held row for its closed item. Supersede pending CI with the corrected final head; do not count the old run as final approval."
  "2026-10-24T09:14:11.717Z",codex-agent,"Candidate-source audit also found that unreadable commit sets with reference-free descriptions could hide a competing commit-only claim. Added six unreadable commit conditions crossed with another valid claim or none (12 controls); all 12 fail against the prior candidate collection, including closures using the other claim. Retain possible commit-only links for every eligible active item when commit evidence is incomplete; use the known merge time to exclude only provably pre-criteria claims. Explicit valid delivery tags keep their existing attribution role. The earlier stale-review correction passed 164/164 focused tests at exact closeout coverage, pinned PM selection 62/62 and native Bun 1.3.5 selection 62/62; an isolated action-only reversion failed ERR_ASSERTION and restoration passed 1/1. Final combined source is now frozen for validation."
  "2026-10-24T09:22:57.811Z",codex-agent,"Final combined regressions pass: focused closeout command node --test test/closeout.test.ts test/closeout-selection.test.ts test/closeout-attribution.test.ts = 176/176, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 for closeout.ts. Pinned pm test selection = 74/74; native Bun 1.3.5 selection = 74/74. Latest compiled workflow hold/unarmed/no-op controls = 3/3. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero source duplication and privacy passed. Isolated fix-only retention-guard reversion failed 12/12 commit-only controls (including one closure instead of zero), restoration passed 12/12. Isolated action-only reversion failed the stale-review regression with ERR_ASSERTION, restoration passed 1/1. Together with the prior function-only 20-case, count-guard 4-case and auto-merge-request proofs these cover both classes. Main advanced only for release metadata; merge it and regenerate the changelog inside the merge before final CI. Earlier superseded CI runs are not final-head approval."
  "2026-10-24T09:27:12.156Z",codex-agent,"Merged origin/main release 2026.10.24 with the merge still pending; regenerated CHANGELOG.md inside the merge and its check passed. Release metadata changes only index version, manifest/package versions and changelog; closeout implementation and regression source are unchanged from the 176/176 focused, 74/74 PM-linked and 74/74 native Bun receipts. Post-merge typecheck, lint and build passed. Strict pm health including required merge drivers passed with no merge-receipt reconciliation needed. Both classes and all identified candidate-source gaps are implemented and verified locally; final immutable npm/Bun CI will validate the merge head. Final CI receipts will be retained in PR 174 body and the final summary. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; release the claim at handoff, never close it."
  "2026-10-24T10:10:12.774Z",codex-agent,"Integration audit of the new null-timestamp selection found that confirmed unmerged PRs can reach the workflow incomplete-merge refusal even when another PR uniquely delivers the item. Separate known-unmerged routine skips from incomplete evidence about potentially merged PRs, and add an actual workflow regression with an unmerged reference plus a valid merged delivery. This preserves the prior since-range behavior while retaining unknown merge timestamps. Supersede old CI only after reproducing this integration regression; do not treat earlier results as approval for the correction."
  "2026-10-24T10:32:28.062Z",codex-agent,"Known-unmerged integration regression verified and fixed: raw false merge status is a routine not_merged skip, distinct from incomplete evidence about possibly merged PRs. Both CLI compaction and workflow summary count it; the workflow can publish the unique merged delivery. Final-source focused closeout suite passed 176/176 with exact 100/100/100/100; held/unarmed/no-op/known-unmerged workflow controls passed 4/4. New filtered workflow command is linked and pinned pm test --run passed 1/1. Reverted only the confirmed-unmerged classifier, rebuilt the package, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"confirmed unmerged references\" test/closeout-workflow.test.ts: ERR_ASSERTION exit 1, publication refused with 1 instead of expected 0. Restored classifier, rebuilt, and passed 1/1. Existing ambiguity, commit-only and auto-merge revert proofs remain recorded above. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and build passed; final immutable CI will certify all-source coverage and native Bun on the corrected head. No PM CLI/SDK defect was found. Keep the item in progress; release the claim for orchestrator verification without closing it."
  "2026-10-24T11:49:11.401Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: audit all closeout read-to-write decisions, bind delivery selection and close provenance to the selected item revision, and exercise peer edits with real SDK mutations in a non-git tracker. Remote branch and main are current; pinned SDK remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T11:57:13.246Z",codex-agent,"SDK audit: pinned 2026.10.20 exposes no expectedRevision/ifUnchanged on close or BulkItemCloseMutation; BulkItemUpdateMutation.match applies only to updates, and runWithItemMutationPrecondition is internal, not a public export. Use public runWithActiveExtensions plus setActiveExtensionHooks beforeMutation to compare hashDocument(context.before) inside the SDK per-item lock before persistence. This preserves normal close validation, workflow policy, history and atomic close evidence. Needed upstream API: close(id, reason, { expectedItemHash }, clientOptions), checked under the same item lock with a stable revision-conflict refusal. Retry selection only for the conflicted item once. Audit: tags, links, criteria chronology, status, comments and body are read-only inputs covered by the exact document hash; close writes completed_at, resolution, expected_result, actual_result and close_reason together. No independent tag/link/comment/criteria mutation path exists in closeout."
  "2026-10-24T12:07:08.618Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: restored only closeout.ts from the PR head before this revision, kept the regression test, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"retag at 1:pull\" test/closeout-revision.test.ts. Result: 0 pass, 1 fail; stale closure selected PR 1 after delivery-pr became PR 2 (assertion 1 !== 2). Restored the fix and reran the identical command: 1 pass, 0 fail. The guard now also covers SDK implicit dependent unblocking; concurrent prerequisite edits cannot be overwritten, and refused dependent writes receive one fresh delivery selection or an explicit hold."
  "2026-10-24T12:08:24.709Z",codex-agent,"Final-source guard-only revert proof in an isolated source copy (active gate source unchanged): removed only the under-lock hash comparison, retained all observers, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"retag at 1:pull|dependent update: changed\" test/closeout-revision.test.ts. Both failed (0/2): stale PR 1 provenance after retag to PR 2, and a peer prerequisite edit overwritten by automatic unblock (open instead of blocked). Restoring only that comparison passed 2/2. The ordinary SDK close lock and lifecycle implementation were real in both runs."
  "2026-10-24T12:15:43.152Z",codex-agent,"The pinned PM-linked node --test test/closeout-revision.test.ts run passed 109/109 with zero failures, skips or cancellations. Further audit found a document/history read boundary: a peer SDK update writes the item before appending history while retaining its lock. Acceptance chronology now uses verifyHistoryEntries(history, selectedDocument), so a new document cannot borrow the previous revision criteria cutoff. A real-SDK history_append scheduling barrier exercises this partial-write boundary. The superseded local broad gate was stopped before changing source; only final-source receipts will be used."
  "2026-10-24T12:17:28.572Z",codex-agent,"History-binding revert proof: in an isolated source copy changed only verifyHistoryEntries(history, selectedDocument) back to verifyHistoryEntries(history), retained the real SDK partial-write scheduling barrier, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"binds acceptance history\" test/closeout-revision.test.ts. Reverted: 0 pass, 1 fail (closed 1 instead of 0 using an older criteria cutoff for the newer document). Restored: 1 pass, 0 fail. The final local targeted command covers all four closeout suites and enforces exact 100/100/100/100 coverage for closeout.ts."
  "2026-10-24T12:19:39.759Z",codex-agent,"Final-source local validation passed: the PM-linked c8 --100 command ran all four closeout suites, 286/286 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exact 100/100/100/100 for closeout.ts. The revision suite contributes 110 tests, including 17-by-6 peer-edit boundaries, bounded retry, guard isolation, removed snapshots, implicit dependent updates and document/history binding. Typecheck, build, test typecheck and lint passed; docstrings, zero-duplication, privacy and canonical changelog checks passed. Strict health with required merge drivers passed with isolated HOME; ambient global extension version skew is absent in the CI-equivalent environment. PM test-result storage is disabled by existing policy, so this comment retains the receipt. Full npm/Bun release evidence will come from CI on the pushed head; thresholds and dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T13:52:01.374Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: reproduce selected-delivery publication refusal, then derive all candidate rows from one item decision: chosen, superseded informational, or blocking hold. Add a 3 x 6 x 2 end-to-end decision table through the actual workflow publication gate, including peer retags. Record behavioral revert proof; run targeted tests, typecheck and lint locally, and require npm plus Bun full release gates in CI on the pushed head."
  "2026-10-24T13:57:57.687Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced the exact round-3 blocker before editing runtime source: the explicit-delivery/missing-merge-SHA/no-peer end-to-end test fails ERR_ASSERTION with exit 1 because the real workflow rejects incomplete merged-PR metadata after local closeout. ItemDecision now projects chosen or blocking-hold outcomes across every candidate; all nonchosen candidates become duplicate_selection informational rows, regardless of original evidence failures. Failed chosen checks and SDK refusals hold all peers. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. The 36-cell workflow matrix and existing non-git SDK suites are running."
  "2026-10-24T14:06:16.808Z",codex-agent,"Focused PM-linked c8 verification passed 286/286 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips, with exact 100/100/100/100 for closeout.ts. Exact command: node node_modules/c8/bin/c8.js --100 --include=closeout.ts --reporter=text --reporter=json --reports-dir=coverage/closeout-revision --temp-directory=coverage/closeout-revision-v8 node --test test/closeout.test.ts test/closeout-attribution.test.ts test/closeout-selection.test.ts test/closeout-revision.test.ts. Existing result-storage policy is disabled; this comment retains the receipt. The peer-retag table explicitly allows a safe hold when a peer invalidates the selected document/history revision before attribution; explicit re-selection with a valid retag closes with fresh provenance."
  "2026-10-24T14:07:20.953Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 fix-only behavioral revert proof: restored only closeout.ts to 4874023 (the pre-round-3 runtime, retaining all round-2 revision guards), rebuilt dist with npm run build, and retained the new end-to-end tests plus workflow unchanged. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern='item decision end to end: explicit delivery tag / (missing merge SHA|failed evidence fetch) / none' test/closeout-workflow.test.ts. Reverted result: 0/2 passed, 2 ERR_ASSERTION failures, exit 1. Both regressions fail at the workflow publication gate after closeout rather than at load/build: incomplete merge or unavailable evidence leaves a fatal competing refusal. Restored the fix byte-for-byte, rebuilt, then ran the same command through pm test --run --only-index 9 --progress with isolated HOME and Git configuration: 2/2 passed, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exit 0. No tests, workflow gates or thresholds were reverted."
  "2026-10-24T14:10:59.424Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 final local validation: PM-linked node --test --test-name-pattern='item decision end to end' test/closeout-workflow.test.ts passed 36/36, zero failures/cancellations/skips (3 selection sources x 6 competitor states x 2 peer schedules). The decision table independently expects 12 closed-and-published outcomes with chosen provenance and 24 open-and-published holds listing every candidate. The restored two publication regressions passed 2/2 with isolated HOME/Git configuration; the explicit safe-history hold control passed 1/1. Focused c8 passed 286/286 with exact 100/100/100/100 for closeout.ts. npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring, npm run duplication, npm run privacy and changelog generation/check passed. Strict health with required merge drivers passed with isolated HOME; two existing advisory findings do not fail strict health. Source inventory, dependency pins, exclusions and thresholds remain unchanged. The item stays in progress for orchestrator verification, with the claim released before push. Remaining verification is read-only CI: npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22/26, plus native Bun acceptance; exact final-head run URLs/counts will be retained in PR 174 and the handoff. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was encountered in this round."
  "2026-10-24T14:31:43.103Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40101464708 at 30b94f1: both Node 26 jobs passed all 1337 tests with zero test failures, then c8 exhausted its unchanged 8192 MiB heap during coverage aggregation. These are failed release gates, not approval. Reduce redundant matrix fixture initialization and unrelated repeated workflow steps while retaining all 36 actual closeout/publication-gate cases, public provenance assertions and the existing full workflow controls. Keep all source/coverage thresholds, heap resources and dependency pins unchanged; rerun focused proof and exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-24T14:34:26.606Z",codex-agent,"All four first-head CI release jobs failed during aggregation at the unchanged 8 GiB heap; the existing broader follow-up pm-github-vhi6 now retains that receipt. Matrix harness optimization reuses four immutable input baselines and executes the unchanged workflow reset before each cell, with fresh PR receipts so an earlier publication cannot satisfy a later cell. Every cell still runs the real CLI, actual closeout refusal gate, publication privacy gates, leased Git push, and public body/provenance assertions. Existing full workflow tests continue to own changelog, strict-health, credential and dispatch controls. No runtime source or workflow gate is changed by this optimization."
  "2026-10-24T14:38:10.086Z",codex-agent,"Optimized-harness revert proof repeated with independent fixture reset before each cell: only closeout.ts restored to 4874023 and rebuilt, retaining current matrix/workflow. The same two-test publication command failed 0/2 passed, exit 1, both ERR_ASSERTION errors at the expected workflow gates: incomplete merged-PR metadata and unavailable head evidence. Restoring the fix byte-for-byte and rebuilding leaves runtime source identical to 30b94f1. This additionally proves a failed earlier case cannot contaminate the next case's evidence. The optimized 36-cell matrix and restored controls are running through PM with isolated HOME/Git configuration; thresholds, heap resources and workflow code remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T14:43:27.629Z",codex-agent,"Final optimized-harness local receipt: PM-linked 36-cell matrix passed 36/36 with zero failures/cancellations/skips and the same 12 closed-and-published / 24 open-and-published-hold expectations. The independent-reset fix-only revert fails both expected publication-gate assertions (0/2, exit 1); restored PM-linked controls pass 2/2 (exit 0). Both PM runs used isolated HOME and Git configuration. Test typecheck, lint, production typecheck and docstrings pass; privacy and changelog checks pass. Runtime source is byte-identical to 30b94f1, whose four CI test phases each passed 1337/1337 before aggregation failed. This follow-up changes only matrix setup and evidence/docs; scripts/coverage-gate.ts, package files, workflow code, source inventory, exclusions, four 100% thresholds and 8192 MiB heap remain unchanged. Release the claim before the follow-up push; retain final exact-head CI receipts in PR 174 and the handoff. Broader aggregation work remains open as pm-github-vhi6."
  "2026-10-24T15:03:21.409Z",codex-agent,"Second exact-head CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40103921945 at ad2e7cb: completed npm Node 26 and Bun Node 22 test phases each pass 1337/1337, then c8 again exhausts the unchanged 8192 MiB heap. The gates remain failed. Four shared callers still repeated package setup for every cell; prepare each immutable baseline once and execute only the real branch preparation, closeout and publication steps per cell. Preserve independent resets, fresh PR receipts, all 36 cases and every outcome/provenance assertion. Keep runtime source, actual workflow code, coverage resources and thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T15:10:02.206Z",codex-agent,"Prepared-baseline matrix local run passed 36/36, zero failures/cancellations/skips, in about 100 seconds. Setup now runs once for four immutable baseline callers; each case restores its input and prepared workflow-owned setup/environment, clears PR receipts, and executes the real Prepare sync branch, Close delivered tracker items and Commit gated closeout changes steps. The real publication privacy/refusal gates and leased push remain inside those unchanged steps. Repeating the runtime-only revert against the prepared harness fails 0/2 passed at the two expected workflow gates (exit 1); runtime was restored byte-for-byte and rebuilt. Final PM-linked matrix/restored controls are running with isolated HOME/Git configuration. Production source and gate configuration remain identical to 30b94f1."
  "2026-10-24T15:12:48.722Z",codex-agent,"Final prepared-baseline PM receipt: 36/36 matrix tests pass with zero failures/cancellations/skips; all 12 closed-and-published and 24 open-and-published-hold expectations remain asserted. PM-linked restored publication controls pass 2/2; runtime-only revert fails 0/2 at the expected gates, exit 1. The matrix runs actual package/scope setup once per four immutable baselines and restores workflow-owned setup/environment plus independent tracker input before every actual branch-preparation, closeout and publication attempt. Fresh receipts prohibit stale publication from satisfying a case. Production source, coverage script, package files and workflows remain unchanged from 30b94f1; typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstrings pass. Both earlier CI runs passed all 1337 tests in all four jobs but failed coverage aggregation, recorded on pm-github-vhi6. No gate resource, inventory, exclusion or threshold is relaxed. Release claim before push; final exact-head full-gate evidence remains read-only CI and will be retained in PR 174 and handoff."
  "2026-10-24T15:42:24.111Z",codex-agent,"The prepared 36-cell matrix and runtime-only revert proof remain unchanged and passing. CI cff0f1c established the complete npm Node 22 gate at the old heap, while Node 26 again passed all 1337 tests and failed aggregation. To complete the requested full-gate evidence, only c8's merge heap ceiling is raised to 12288 MiB on the existing public 16 GB runners. There is no coverage threshold, source inventory, ignore list, dependency or workflow change. The real coverage-gate suite passes 9/9 via PM, including full/partial receipt and flag-routing controls; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Release both claims before push; final exact-head CI URL/counts will be retained in PR 174 and handoff. Broader bounded aggregation remains tracked by pm-github-vhi6 and neither item is closed."
